1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,700
W1: I can't believe how busy we've been.

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:06,505
We've received so many orders in the past few days.

3
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:14,710
W2: Because it's the holiday season, we probably won't get much of a break for the next couple of months.

4
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:23,960
W1: Everyone has been at the office long after normal working hours have finished this week, so I've heard several complaints.

5
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,400
Can't we hire any more workers?

6
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:30,460
W2: I'd love to, but I'm not sure if that's possible.

7
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,780
What do you think, Greg?

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,540
M: That's already been taken care of.

9
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:40,080
You'll be training fifteen temporary employees in your department tomorrow.

10
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,340
W1: Wow, I'm impressed.

11
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:45,885
I've never seen management work this fast before.
